## What is a Class?
A class is a blueprint used to create objects.
Suppose we are going to construct a building so for that a plan is required that plan or blueprint is called as class and buildings constructed based on plan is called object 
•  Class = blueprint 
•  Object = real item(instance)
•  Class variables = common for all objects

## Reference Variable
• A reference variable is a variable that stores the reference (address) of an object.
• It is used to access the object's attributes and methods.

## Object
• An object is an instance of a class.
• It contains its own data (attributes) and can access methods defined in the class.


